'''Kang Roo''' (カ・ンガリュ, ''Ka Ngaryu'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]] and [[Legend Stages]]. It was added in [[Version 1.0 Update|Version 1.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Kang Roo
|image = E 010.png
|first appearance = '''EoC''': [[Bermuda (Empire of Cats)|Chapter 1 - Bermuda/Tokyo]]<br>
'''ItF''': [[Spain (Into the Future)|Chapter 1 - Spain]]<br>
'''CotC''': [[Mercury (Cats of the Cosmos)|Chapter 1 - Mercury]]<br>
'''SoL''': [[Churros Night|Sub-chapter 2 - Churros Night]]
|money drop = 1,400¢ - 5,530¢
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Floating Bus Stop|Sub-chapter 19 - Floating Bus Stop]]
}}

==Enemy==
A strong, heavy-hitting enemy that does a significant amount of damage to a single [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]] quickly. Due to the speed at which they attack, multiple Kang Roos can knock your cats back continually before they're able to attack in return, resulting in this enemy being quite a formidable foe early on.

Kang Roos have a high money drop and become relatively easy to kill as you progress through the game, so they can serve as good money sources.

==Strategy==
Even though this enemy looks formidable, it is actually very easy if alone. It has powerful attacks, but they are Single Target, making it easy to deal with when encountered without any support. If you really have trouble with this enemy, use [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]] with [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Basic Cats]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cats]]. If you have a problem in Chapter 3, use [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]].

Later on, Kang Roo is easier to deal with and becomes a source of large amounts of money.

