==Trivia==
*Kang is a Chinese and Korean surname. Since surnames come first in these languages  (e.g., [[wikipedia:Kang Hui (news anchor)|Kang Hui]], [[Wikipedia:Kang Yu-chan|Kang Yu-chan]]), it's possible that Kang is actually Kang Roo's last name.
*Kang Roo's Japanese description references the manga ''[[wikipedia:Ashita no Joe|Ashita no Joe]]'', stating that a manga inspired it to start boxing and that it tragically burned out in pure white, which refers to the last words of the protagonist, [[wikia:joe:Joe Yabuki|Joe Yabuki]], in the series: "I burned my fire until there was nothing left. All that's left is pure white ash." In the often-parodied [https://web.archive.org/web/20220808143623im_/https://i0.wp.com/white-ash.net/whistle/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/tomorrows-Joe-20-259-Joe-ending-.png?w=534&ssl=1 final panel], Joe is shown sitting down with white hair after he fought [[wikia:joe:Jose Mendoza|José Mendoza]], whose hair also prematurely turned white from trauma.
*It attacks in the same way as [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Welterweight Cat]], another character who references ''Ashita no Joe''.
*In the [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English version]], Kang Roo was referred to using masculine pronouns, yet in real life, only female kangaroos have pouches.
*Before [[Version 6.0 Update|Version 6.0]] gave Kang Roo Multi-Hit, its 250 damage was in a single hit on the 10th frame of its attack animation.

